    en: "<p>Recall from the previous modules:</p><ul><li>A <strong>program</strong> is an ordered set of instructions telling the computer what to do, step by step.</li><li>The computer does not understand intentions; it carries out literally what was written.</li><li>Software has three kinds, and the programs you will write are <strong>application software</strong>.</li><li>Python is <strong>open source</strong> and free, which is why it spread through universities and hospitals.</li></ul><p>You need no mathematics here beyond addition and comparison, and you will write no code in this module: this is a thinking stop before the doing stop.</p>"
